{"author":{"id":"ad87ffa09351c4e5a412ec8ee1546e86b314f33d6f28629bb4bcfe7b2290924d"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794309822,"nonce":"VjbD6BpjkIJNQnjiEWXZAs8IkSs=","title":"Analysis offsets are code points; the reader and API read them as UTF-16 units","message":"Token and sentence start/end come from Stanza's start_char/end_char (analysis/src/skolia_analysis/parsers/stanza_parser.py:85), Python str indices: code points. The reader slices the text with them (Reader.svelte sentenceText, highlighting) and the API checks cloze blanks against sentence.length, both UTF-16 units. They agree inside the BMP; each character outside it (emoji, 𝔐) shifts every later offset by one. ADR 0002 says the cloze offsets are JavaScript string indices, which isn't what the analysis gives. Fix in the analysis (emit UTF-16 offsets) with an analyzer version bump; the reader reads every stored version, so it needs to know which unit an analysis uses.","files":null}]}